Writing \(S=J_s\), the controlled loci are
\[
\begin{aligned}
\mathcal F&=\{\exists n:\ Sn=0,\ D,h\parallel n\},\\
\mathcal U&=\{\exists n:\ S=aI+(b-a)nn^T,\ D,h\parallel n\},\\
\mathcal X&=\{D=h=0\}.
\end{aligned}
\]
The algebraic residual set is
\[
\mathcal R=\mathcal P\setminus(\mathcal F\cup\mathcal U\cup\mathcal X).
\]
The report gives the symmetry proofs, transformation conditions, range restrictions for dualities, and the assumptions behind each controlled result. The rank-one bound on commuting on-site charges does not bound emergent sectors.

I completed 108 screening cases and stored 710 momentum/parity spectral blocks, reaching \(L=22\), within about 37 minutes.

- Ising and XX calibrations gave energy estimates \(c=0.499998\) and \(0.999939\).
- An interacting single-\(Z_2\) candidate gave \(c_{\rm chord}(22)=0.50610\), with spectra and energy fits consistent with Ising criticality.
- Other candidates gave chord estimates \(1.19481\) and \(1.40121\). Their half-chain entropy growth disagreed with those values, so neither is a measured central charge.
- Near the symmetry-free candidate, the soft-mode curvature stayed approximately constant across \(L=16,20,22\), consistent with a quadratic threshold. Three sizes do not establish its thermodynamic exponent.

No scale-consistent \(c>1\) point was established. No general exclusion was proved for \(\mathcal R\).

